 "verdict": "Pace is a real but MODEST variance lever: across the observed NBA pace range (~92-104) the same matchup's upset prob shifts by only a few points -- fewer possessions favor the underdog (sqrt(N) scaling), but the effect is small because real pace varies little. A 60% favorite: upset prob 39.8% at pace 104 vs 40.4% at pace 92 (slow-minus-fast swing +0.6 pts). A 70% favorite: upset prob 29.6% at pace 104 vs 30.7% at pace 92 (slow-minus-fast swing +1.1 pts). A 80% favorite: upset prob 19.5% at pace 104 vs 20.9% at pace 92 (slow-minus-fast swing +1.4 pts).",
